&lt;h3&gt;


  About the Author
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm &lt;strong&gt;Mustafa Morbel&lt;/strong&gt; — Senior Frontend Engineer with over 17 years of experience crafting high-performance React architectures, WebGL applications, and developer tooling.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find full component examples and open-source boilerplates on my &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/mkare" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub (@mkare)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://linkedin.com/in/mustafamorbel" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and follow along on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://x.com/mustafamorbel" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;X / Twitter (@mustafamorbel)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; for React &amp;amp; TypeScript best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a custom hook you use in every project? Share it in the comments below, and leave a few claps if you found this guide helpful!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You're building the frontend for a store. The design is ready, but the backend isn't, and you're tired of hardcoding &lt;code&gt;const products = [...]&lt;/code&gt; in a file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In this tutorial we'll build a small React product page against a free mock REST API, with &lt;strong&gt;no backend, no API key and no signup&lt;/strong&gt;. By the end you'll have:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a product list with &lt;strong&gt;search and pagination&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;each product's &lt;strong&gt;category and reviews&lt;/strong&gt; loaded in the same request&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a "create product" form that shows &lt;strong&gt;real validation errors&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a way to test your &lt;strong&gt;loading and error states&lt;/strong&gt; on demand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Disclosure: I built &lt;a href="https://www.devseedapi.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;DevSeed API&lt;/a&gt;, the mock API used here. It's free, and I'd love feedback on it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Look at the data
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every endpoint is a plain &lt;code&gt;GET&lt;/code&gt; you can open in the browser:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;https://www.devseedapi.com/api/v1/ecommerce/products?limit=2
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"success"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"data"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"p1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Wireless Mouse"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"price"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;29.99&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"categoryId"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"c1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"createdAt"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"2026-03-02T10:00:00Z"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"p2"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Mechanical Keyboard"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"price"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;79.99&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"categoryId"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"c1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"createdAt"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"2026-03-02T10:10:00Z"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"meta"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"total"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;120&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"page"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"limit"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"totalPages"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;60&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The e-commerce set also has &lt;code&gt;categories&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;reviews&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;orders&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;cart&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;coupons&lt;/code&gt;, and there are user and SaaS datasets too. Every list endpoint supports the same query params:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Example&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Pagination&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;?page=2&amp;amp;limit=10&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Search&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;?search=mouse&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Exact filter&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;?categoryId=c1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Range filter&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;?minPrice=20&amp;amp;maxPrice=50&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Sort&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;?sortBy=price&amp;amp;order=asc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Related data&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;?include=category,reviews&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;They combine, so &lt;code&gt;?search=mouse&amp;amp;maxPrice=50&amp;amp;sortBy=price&amp;amp;order=asc&lt;/code&gt; returns the mouse-related products under $50, cheapest first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  2. Load related data in one request
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the part most mock APIs skip. On a real product page you need the product's category and its reviews, and you don't want to fire three requests and join them yourself.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight http"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;GET https://www.devseedapi.com/api/v1/ecommerce/products/p1?include&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;reviews&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"success"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"data"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"p1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Wireless Mouse"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"price"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;29.99&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"categoryId"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"c1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"category"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"c1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Computer Accessories"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"reviews"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;101&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"productId"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"p1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"userId"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"u1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"rating"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"comment"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Excellent mouse!"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;163&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"productId"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"p1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"userId"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"u70"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"rating"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"comment"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Exactly as described."&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;(Trimmed a little for space.) &lt;code&gt;include&lt;/code&gt; works on list endpoints too, which is what we'll use next.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  3. A product list with search and pagination
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Set up a React app (&lt;code&gt;npm create vite@latest shop -- --template react&lt;/code&gt;) and add a small hook:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// useProducts.js&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;API&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://www.devseedapi.com/api/v1/ecommerce"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;LOADING&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"loading"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;simulate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// One string describing the request; a new value means a new fetch.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;simulate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setResult&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;controller&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AbortController&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;URLSearchParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;limit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;include&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"category,reviews"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;parse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`${API}/products?${params}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;signal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;controller&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;signal&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`HTTP ${res.status}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setResult&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"success"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"AbortError"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setResult&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"error"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;controller&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;abort&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Until the response for the current request arrives, we're loading.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;LOADING&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;And the page:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ProductList.jsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useProducts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"./useProducts"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;average&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;reviews&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;reviews&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;reviews&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;reduce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;rating&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;reviews&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toFixed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"–"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProductList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setSearch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;placeholder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Search products"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setSearch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"loading"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Loading&lt;/span&gt;…&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"error"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"alert"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Couldn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'t load products: {error}&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;}

      &amp;lt;ul&amp;gt;
        {products.map(p =&amp;gt; (
          &amp;lt;li key={p.id}&amp;gt;
            &amp;lt;strong&amp;gt;{p.name}&amp;lt;/strong&amp;gt; · ${p.price} · {p.category?.name} · ★ {average(p.reviews)} ({p.reviews.length})
          &amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;
        ))}
      &amp;lt;/ul&amp;gt;

      {meta &amp;amp;&amp;amp; (
        &amp;lt;nav&amp;gt;
          &amp;lt;button disabled={page &amp;lt;= 1} onClick={() =&amp;gt; setPage(page - 1)}&amp;gt;Previous&amp;lt;/button&amp;gt;
          &amp;lt;span&amp;gt; Page {meta.page} of {meta.totalPages} &amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;
          &amp;lt;button disabled={page &amp;gt;= meta.totalPages} onClick={() =&amp;gt; setPage(page + 1)}&amp;gt;Next&amp;lt;/button&amp;gt;
        &amp;lt;/nav&amp;gt;
      )}
    &amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;
  )
}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Each product arrives with its &lt;code&gt;category&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;reviews&lt;/code&gt; already attached, so there's no second round of requests. &lt;code&gt;meta.totalPages&lt;/code&gt; drives the pagination buttons.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  4. A create form with real validation errors
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mock APIs usually accept anything you &lt;code&gt;POST&lt;/code&gt;, so your error handling never gets exercised. Here, writes are &lt;strong&gt;validated like a real API but never stored&lt;/strong&gt;: the response shows the record that would have been created.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Send a bad body:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;curl -X POST https://www.devseedapi.com/api/v1/ecommerce/products \
  -H &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Content-Type: application/json"&lt;/span&gt; \
  -d &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'{"name":"Desk Lamp","price":"cheap"}'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"success"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"message"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Validation failed"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"errors"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"field"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"price"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"message"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"must be a number"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"field"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"categoryId"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"message"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"is required"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That's a &lt;code&gt;422&lt;/code&gt;. It even checks references: &lt;code&gt;"categoryId": "c999"&lt;/code&gt; fails with &lt;code&gt;no categories record with id "c999"&lt;/code&gt;. A valid body returns &lt;code&gt;201&lt;/code&gt; with a new id and a &lt;code&gt;Location&lt;/code&gt; header.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A form that maps those errors onto fields:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// NewProductForm.jsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;API&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://www.devseedapi.com/api/v1/ecommerce"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;NewProductForm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setForm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;categoryId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"c1"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;fieldErrors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setFieldErrors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;created&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setCreated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;preventDefault&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setFieldErrors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCreated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`${API}/products`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"POST"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Content-Type"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"application/json"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;422&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setFieldErrors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fromEntries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;errors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCreated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;field&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setForm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;fieldErrors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;small&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"crimson"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;fieldErrors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;small&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;onSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"price"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"categoryId"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;created&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Created&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;created&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;created&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Leave the price empty or type a category that doesn't exist, and you'll see the server's message under the right field. &lt;code&gt;PUT&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;PATCH&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;DELETE&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;/products/:id&lt;/code&gt; work the same way.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  5. Test your loading and error states
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The happy path is easy. The states that break in production are the slow request and the failed one, and they're hard to trigger against a real backend. Three query params do it:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Param&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Effect&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;delay=2000&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;waits 2 seconds before responding&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;error=503&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;always responds with that status&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;errorRate=30&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;fails 30% of requests with a &lt;code&gt;500&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our hook already passes extra params through, so:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// See the spinner for 2 seconds&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;simulate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2000&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// See the error state&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;simulate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;503&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Flaky network: does a retry button or a stale list still look right?&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;simulate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;errorRate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;30&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;error=503&lt;/code&gt; case returns &lt;code&gt;{ "success": false, "message": "Simulated API Error" }&lt;/code&gt; with a 503 status, so the component shows "Couldn't load products: Simulated API Error". This is also handy for Storybook stories and Playwright/Cypress tests of your error UI.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Swapping in the real backend later
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When your backend is ready, change &lt;code&gt;API&lt;/code&gt; to point at it. If your real API uses the same ideas (&lt;code&gt;page&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;limit&lt;/code&gt;, a &lt;code&gt;meta&lt;/code&gt; object, field-level &lt;code&gt;422&lt;/code&gt; errors), the components barely change. If it doesn't, the mock gives you a concrete contract to discuss with your backend team.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A few honest limits: writes are never saved, so a &lt;code&gt;POST&lt;/code&gt; won't appear in the next &lt;code&gt;GET&lt;/code&gt;. The data is the same for everyone, and there's a rate limit of 200 requests per 15 minutes per client.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Wrap-up
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We built a product list with search, pagination and related data in a single request, a form that handles real validation errors, and a way to test loading and failure states, all against a free API with no setup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Docs and a live console for every endpoint: &lt;a href="https://www.devseedapi.com/docs/ecommerce/products" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://www.devseedapi.com/docs/ecommerce/products&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://github.com/gayashanacd/dev-seed-api" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/gayashanacd/dev-seed-api&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If there's a dataset you'd want next (social media, fintech, edtech…), or something that annoyed you, &lt;a href="https://tally.so/r/Z9OMa0?page=devto" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;tell me here&lt;/a&gt;. It takes under a minute, and it decides what gets built next.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Disclosure: I work on Skillselion, an independent directory of Claude Code, Codex and Cursor extensions. We are not affiliated with HeyGen, Remotion or Anthropic. This post was drafted with AI help, and every quote was checked against the linked source.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you want Claude Code to write a video for you, the two obvious stacks are HyperFrames and Remotion. Both publish official agent skills, and the main skill of each has about 850,000 installs or more. It is tempting to start with the rendering model. I would start with the license, because for many teams it settles the question before any code runs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The short answer
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;HyperFrames ships under Apache 2.0, so any company can use it commercially. Remotion is free for individuals, non-profits and for-profit companies with up to 3 employees; everyone else needs a paid Company License. If you are a React team that fits the free tier or will pay for a Company License, Remotion is a strong fit. If you want an agent to write the whole video from a prompt, or your company is larger, HyperFrames is the easier call.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What does the Remotion license actually say?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is from Remotion's LICENSE.md. Free use covers:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;an individual&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a for-profit organization with up to 3 employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a non-profit or not-for-profit organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;someone evaluating Remotion who is not yet using it commercially&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And for everyone else: "You are required to obtain a Company License to use Remotion if you are not within the group of entities eligible for a Free License." (Source: remotion-dev/remotion, LICENSE.md at e6b9083, line 43.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same file says the license will change slightly in Remotion 5.0. The open pull request for that change (remotion-dev/remotion#3750) counts contractors toward team size, so check the version you install.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;HyperFrames uses the Apache License 2.0 with no company-size limit. Two of its nine skills (reverse-any-video and style-sampling) are marked "HyperFrames Pro" in the README, so read that line before you plan around them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How does each one turn code into frames?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Remotion gives each component a frame number and lets React render it. Code reads like an app: useCurrentFrame(), props, components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;HyperFrames keeps one paused GSAP timeline and seeks it to each frame. Code reads like a web page with timing attributes such as data-start and data-duration. Its core skill states the contract plainly: "No Date.now(), unseeded Math.random(), network fetches, timers or repeat: -1. Everything visible is a function of timeline time." (Source: heygen-com/hyperframes, skills/hyperframes/SKILL.md at cb2b515, line 25.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That rule suits an agent. One that writes clean HTML can write a scene, and &lt;code&gt;npx hyperframes check --json&lt;/code&gt; reports most contract violations with a Fix: line before you render.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How are the agent skills organised?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;HyperFrames:&lt;/strong&gt; nine skills split by job. The &lt;a href="https://skillselion.com/skills/heygen-com/hyperframes?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=social&amp;amp;utm_campaign=hyperframes-vs-remotion-devto" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;HyperFrames core skill&lt;/a&gt; holds the rules, and hyperframes-cli, hyperframes-registry and media-use handle rendering, ready-made blocks and media.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Remotion:&lt;/strong&gt; thirteen skills in remotion-dev/skills, with the &lt;a href="https://skillselion.com/skills/remotion-dev/skills/remotion-best-practices?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=social&amp;amp;utm_campaign=hyperframes-vs-remotion-devto" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Remotion best practices router skill&lt;/a&gt; in front. Its description is one line: "Router for all Remotion skills".&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On 19 November 2026 the Skillselion catalog API (skills.sh registry data) showed more than 1.5 million lifetime installs for the HyperFrames core skill and about 850,000 for the Remotion router. Those are registry install events, so treat them as a reach signal, not as a count of active users.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Can you move a Remotion project across?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Partly. HyperFrames publishes a &lt;a href="https://skillselion.com/skills/heygen-com/hyperframes/remotion-to-hyperframes?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=social&amp;amp;utm_campaign=hyperframes-vs-remotion-devto" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;remotion-to-hyperframes migration skill&lt;/a&gt; that translates a composition and then compares it to the original frame by frame with &lt;code&gt;npx hyperframes diff&lt;/code&gt;. Its lint step names what will not come across: useState, useReducer, useEffect with dependencies, async calculateMetadata and React UI kits such as MUI or shadcn "don't translate". A project built mostly from Sequence, interpolate and spring ports well. One built on stateful React UI does not.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Which one I would pick
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your team writes React and reuses app components in video, and you fit the free tier or will pay for a Company License: Remotion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your company has more than 3 employees and does not want a paid license: HyperFrames.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want an agent to write the whole video from a prompt, with a check and diff loop: HyperFrames.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You already have Remotion work: run remotion-to-hyperframes on one composition and read its TRANSLATION_NOTES.md before you commit to a move.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The full comparison, with every quote pinned to a commit, is in our &lt;a href="https://skillselion.com/guides/hyperframes-vs-remotion?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=social&amp;amp;utm_campaign=hyperframes-vs-remotion-devto" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;HyperFrames vs Remotion comparison guide&lt;/a&gt;. For the Remotion side in depth, see the &lt;a href="https://skillselion.com/guides/best-remotion-skills-for-claude-code?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=social&amp;amp;utm_campaign=hyperframes-vs-remotion-devto" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;ranked guide to Remotion skills for Claude Code&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Skillselion is a live catalog, refreshed daily from skills.sh, GitHub and MCP registries, ranked by real installs.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We build websites for a living, and most of the motion we ship ends up locked inside client projects. So we pulled thirteen of our favourite patterns out, cleaned them up and put them online for free. They're called Republic UI, they're MIT licensed, and every one installs with a single shadcn command.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can try them all at &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.republicmarketing.co.uk/ui/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;republicmarketing.co.uk/ui&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F75how8y51s0jycws0uq0.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F75how8y51s0jycws0uq0.jpg" alt="Slat Shutter Hero" width="800" height="600"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What's in the set
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Slat Shutter Hero.&lt;/strong&gt; Scroll, and the cover photo splits into vertical slats that part from the centre outwards to reveal a second scene. The headline hands over line by line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Photo Deck.&lt;/strong&gt; A stack of prints you can drag, flick, or step through with the arrows and keyboard. Going back flies the last print in from the left instead of just swapping it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Timeline Scrubber.&lt;/strong&gt; Drag along a month ruler and the photos wipe in the direction you move, while the temperature rolls on digit reels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Testimonial Reel.&lt;/strong&gt; A quote, a portrait that slides up like a reel and a stat that rolls like an odometer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Morph Island.&lt;/strong&gt; A status pill that morphs from idle to uploading, done and a full preview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fan Gallery.&lt;/strong&gt; Photo cards on an arc. Drag it, flick it, tap a side card or use the keys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus a facts hero, feature rows with live UI, a bento of mini interfaces, a torn-paper portrait scroll, a scroll-fill headline, a sector wheel and a scattered-photo about section.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fjf04ybojj0xz8zkfp9mc.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fjf04ybojj0xz8zkfp9mc.jpg" alt="Fan Gallery" width="800" height="600"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Install
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Add the registry to your &lt;code&gt;components.json&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"registries"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"@republic"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://www.republicmarketing.co.uk/ui/r/{name}.json"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then add whatever you need:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx shadcn@latest add @republic/fan-gallery
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Each component is one self-contained file. The only dependencies are &lt;code&gt;motion&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;clsx&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;tailwind-merge&lt;/code&gt; and, for a few, &lt;code&gt;lucide-react&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Five rules we kept coming back to
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These came out of client feedback over the years, and they made more difference than any single effect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Numbers roll, they never cross-fade.&lt;/strong&gt; If a figure changes, it moves on digit reels, fast at first and slow to land. Two values fading over each other reads as a glitch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. One focal point at a time.&lt;/strong&gt; When a new element takes over, the old one leaves properly. Dimmed leftovers peeking from the edge make a small space feel crowded.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. One easing curve, used everywhere.&lt;/strong&gt; Most of the set uses &lt;code&gt;cubic-bezier(0.42, 0, 0, 1)&lt;/code&gt;. Things that share a curve feel like they belong to the same product.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Every interaction has a keyboard path.&lt;/strong&gt; The deck, the timeline and the fan all work with arrow keys, and the timeline also takes Home and End. Autoplay pauses on hover and only runs while the component is on screen.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Test the boring cases.&lt;/strong&gt; Rapid clicks, dragging a few pixels and letting go, resizing the window mid-animation, scrolling back up. Most of our fixes came from these, not from the happy path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F8exmjqkcq0tpp28k3wtr.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F8exmjqkcq0tpp28k3wtr.jpg" alt="Photo Deck" width="800" height="600"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Real images, not grey boxes
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every demo uses original images made for the set, so the components look the way they will in a real build. The images are free to use with the components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Links
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Live demos and install commands: &lt;a href="https://www.republicmarketing.co.uk/ui/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;republicmarketing.co.uk/ui&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source on GitHub: &lt;a href="https://github.com/rm-sjent/republic-ui" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;rm-sjent/republic-ui&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Also on 21st.dev: &lt;a href="https://21st.dev/@sajad" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;21st.dev/@sajad&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you use one in a project, I'd love to see it. And if you want a whole site built with this level of care, that's what we do at &lt;a href="https://www.republicmarketing.co.uk/web-design-london" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Republic Marketing&lt;/a&gt;, a web design agency in London and Birmingham.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every SaaS that offers integrations ends up building the same page. A grid of cards. A &lt;code&gt;Connect&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;Connected&lt;/code&gt; label on each. An OAuth popup. Loading, empty and error states. A refresh after the user disconnects something. And then you maintain all of it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In &lt;code&gt;@bytechef/embedded&lt;/code&gt; 0.4.0 that page ships prebuilt as one React component:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;IntegrationMarketplace&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;jwtToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Each of your users sees the integrations they're allowed to use and connects them right there. The catalog runs in an iframe. The Connect dialog runs in your page, so your own callbacks keep working.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fnp8stl0m5yxjgh4hmst0.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fnp8stl0m5yxjgh4hmst0.png" alt="The Integration Marketplace in the embedded sample app: a grid of Slack and Gmail cards with Connected labels" width="800" height="500"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is part 13 of the ByteChef Embedded series. Below: the setup, the code, how the iframe talks to your page, the API underneath, and the gotchas we hit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  TL;DR
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upgrade to &lt;code&gt;@bytechef/embedded&lt;/code&gt; 0.4.0 or later.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Render &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;IntegrationMarketplace /&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; with a connected user's JWT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In ByteChef: publish an integration, create a configuration for it, and flip the configuration's &lt;strong&gt;Enabled&lt;/strong&gt; switch. In every environment you use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add your app's origin to &lt;code&gt;BYTECHEF_EMBEDDED_ALLOWED_PARENT_ORIGINS&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Where it fits
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ByteChef Embedded now has three ways to put integrations and automations in front of a user:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Hand-built grid (part 1)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Integration Marketplace&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Automation Hub (part 12)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Lists&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Integrations you shipped&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Integrations you shipped&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Automation templates&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;User ends up with&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;An integration instance&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;An integration instance&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A running automation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Rendering&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Your React code&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Iframe from your ByteChef host&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Iframe from your ByteChef host&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Code you write&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Fetch, grid, states, refresh&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One component and a JWT&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One component and a JWT&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On the server the marketplace and a hand-built grid produce the same thing: an integration instance tying the user's connection to one of your integration's configurations. Only who draws the page changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Four things before a card shows up
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An empty marketplace is almost always a setup issue.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Publish an integration
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Switch to the &lt;strong&gt;Development&lt;/strong&gt; environment, open &lt;strong&gt;Embedded → Integrations&lt;/strong&gt; and click &lt;strong&gt;New Integration&lt;/strong&gt;. Pick a Component (Gmail, Salesforce, Slack; it can't be changed later) and a Name. Category, Description, Tags and Permission Expression are optional.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fi4rg6obx028yfam0kg38.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fi4rg6obx028yfam0kg38.png" alt="The Create Integration dialog with Component, Name, Category, Description, Permission Expression and Tags fields" width="800" height="500"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Add at least one workflow, then publish. Publishing freezes the workflows as a numbered, read-only version. Users only ever run published versions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. Enable a configuration
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Publishing alone doesn't list anything. A configuration does: it deploys one published version into one environment, with your OAuth app credentials, the workflows you switch on and their default inputs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Development:&lt;/strong&gt; expand the integration, open its &lt;strong&gt;Configurations&lt;/strong&gt; tab, click &lt;strong&gt;Configure&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Staging / Production:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Embedded → Integration Configurations → New Configuration&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then the step everyone misses: &lt;strong&gt;flip the Enabled switch.&lt;/strong&gt; New configurations start disabled. Each environment has its own list, so the Production marketplace only shows integrations with an enabled Production configuration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fb9xpauyzwt2usch1f7k9.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fb9xpauyzwt2usch1f7k9.png" alt="The Gmail integration on its Configurations tab, with one configuration enabled and its six workflows listed" width="800" height="500"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  3. Decide who sees it
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two expressions control visibility. Both are evaluated against the connected user: &lt;code&gt;metadata&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;externalId&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;email&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;name&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;environment&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The integration's &lt;strong&gt;Permission Expression&lt;/strong&gt; gates the integration. Blank means everyone. Anything that doesn't evaluate to &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt;, including a typo, hides it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The configuration's &lt;strong&gt;Assignment rule&lt;/strong&gt; picks which configuration a self-serve user lands on. If several pass, the highest version wins.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;metadata['plan'] == 'pro' || metadata['plan'] == 'enterprise'
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Your backend sets &lt;code&gt;metadata&lt;/code&gt;, for example with &lt;code&gt;PATCH /api/embedded/v1/me&lt;/code&gt;. Values are strings, so compare against quoted literals.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  4. Allow your app's origin
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;BYTECHEF_EMBEDDED_ALLOWED_PARENT_ORIGINS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;https://app.example.com,https://admin.example.com
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;ByteChef sends this as &lt;code&gt;Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors ...&lt;/code&gt;, and the iframe only accepts its init message from these origins. Scheme, host and port must match exactly. Leave it empty and any site can embed the page (the console warns you).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The code
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The sample app's &lt;code&gt;front-end/src/app/integration-marketplace/page.tsx&lt;/code&gt;, with field mapping trimmed:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'use client'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;IntegrationMarketplace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'@bytechef/embedded'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;getToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'@/lib/api'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;BYTECHEF_APP_BASE_URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;BYTECHEF_ENVIRONMENT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'@/lib/config'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'react'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;IntegrationMarketplacePage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jwtToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setJwtToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;setJwtToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jwtToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"w-full p-4"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"absolute inset-0 flex flex-col bg-muted lg:pl-72"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;header&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"px-4 pt-4"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"text-xl font-semibold"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Integration&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Marketplace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

            &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;IntegrationMarketplace&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="n"&gt;baseUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;BYTECHEF_APP_BASE_URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"min-h-0 flex-1"&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="n"&gt;environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;BYTECHEF_ENVIRONMENT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="n"&gt;jwtToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jwtToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="n"&gt;mapObjectFields&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;mapObjectFields&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;getToken()&lt;/code&gt; asks your backend to sign a connected-user JWT. Never sign it in the browser.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Prop&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Default&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What it does&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;jwtToken&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;required&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The connected user's JWT&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;baseUrl&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;https://app.bytechef.io&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Your ByteChef host&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;environment&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;'PRODUCTION'&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Whose configurations count. Sent as &lt;code&gt;X-Environment&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;className&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;none&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Class for the wrapper. The iframe fills it, so give it a height&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;none&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Colors, font, radius, light or dark&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;mapObjectFields&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;none&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Field-mapping callbacks for the Connect dialog&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;onConnectDialogClose&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;none&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Called when the Connect dialog closes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How the iframe and your page talk
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The component renders &lt;code&gt;${baseUrl}/integration-marketplace.html&lt;/code&gt; and speaks &lt;code&gt;postMessage&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Message&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Direction&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;When&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;EMBED_READY&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;iframe → page&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Loaded, wants parameters&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;EMBED_INIT&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;page → iframe&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Sends JWT, environment, theme. Re-sent when they change&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;EMBED_OPEN_CONNECT_DIALOG&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;iframe → page&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;User clicked Connect or Connected&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;EMBED_INTEGRATIONS_CHANGED&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;page → iframe&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Dialog closed, refetch the catalog&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The iframe has no credentials of its own. It shows loading dots until &lt;code&gt;EMBED_INIT&lt;/code&gt; arrives, then keeps the token in memory. Pass a new token, or a different user signs in on the same tab, and it drops its cache and refetches without reloading the frame.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Both sides check message origins. Your page only opens a dialog for messages from your ByteChef origin &lt;strong&gt;and&lt;/strong&gt; its own iframe window. The iframe only accepts init from an allowed parent origin.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why the Connect dialog opens in your page
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Field mapping is why. &lt;code&gt;mapObjectFields&lt;/code&gt; is made of functions: callbacks that list the remote system's object types and fields live, against the user's own connection.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;mapObjectFields&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Contacts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;objectTypes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="n"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;executeAction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;objects&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;executeAction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'salesforce'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'listObjects'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Array&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
                    &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
                    &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

                &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;objects&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// integrationFields, applicationFields ...&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;postMessage&lt;/code&gt; can't clone functions. So the iframe doesn't open the dialog. It asks your page to, and your page mounts &lt;code&gt;useConnectDialog&lt;/code&gt; with your callbacks right where you defined them, next to your API client and your session. When the dialog closes, the component tells the iframe to refetch, so a card the user just disconnected doesn't keep saying Connected.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Connected&lt;/strong&gt; opens the same dialog in manage mode: switch workflows on and off, edit inputs, or disconnect. Every change saves immediately. Input edits are debounced 600 ms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F5utfl5btsrfmhx2aovyc.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F5utfl5btsrfmhx2aovyc.png" alt="The Connect dialog in manage mode for Gmail, with workflow switches, an INPUTS section and a Disconnect button" width="800" height="500"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  No private API
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The iframe and the dialog call the same endpoints you'd call yourself, under &lt;code&gt;/api/embedded/v1&lt;/code&gt;, with the user's JWT and &lt;code&gt;X-Environment&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Endpoint&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Called by&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Does&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;GET /integrations&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;iframe&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The user's catalog&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;GET /integrations/{id}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;dialog&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One integration, its workflows and the user's instances&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;POST /integrations/{id}/instances&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;dialog&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Connect&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;POST/DELETE /integration-instances/{id}/workflows/{uuid}/enable&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;dialog&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Toggle a workflow&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;PUT /integration-instances/{id}/workflows/{uuid}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;dialog&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Save workflow inputs&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;DELETE /integration-instances/{id}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;dialog&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Disconnect&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An empty &lt;code&gt;integrationInstances&lt;/code&gt; array in the catalog response means Connect. Anything else means Connected.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A few server behaviors worth knowing:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Assignment rule is checked once, at connect.&lt;/strong&gt; Existing instances keep their configuration, so enabling a newer configuration later doesn't move anybody.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Disconnect doesn't break automations.&lt;/strong&gt; ByteChef deletes the instance and its workflow settings. If the connection is still used elsewhere, it keeps it as one of the user's own connections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Every endpoint has a backend twin&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;GET /{externalUserId}/integrations&lt;/code&gt; and so on), authenticated with your environment's API secret key. Use those for admin views and server jobs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Build your own, or don't
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our sample app keeps both versions side by side: part one's hand-built grid and the marketplace, on the same data.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwhnczn1gwwgrun9lko6g.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwhnczn1gwwgrun9lko6g.png" alt="The hand-built Integrations page in the sample app, with Other category badges and Connected labels" width="800" height="500"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hand-built one shows the cost of owning the contract. It read a &lt;code&gt;title&lt;/code&gt; field the API doesn't return, so its cards had no headings until we fixed it. Its badge still reads &lt;code&gt;category&lt;/code&gt;, which the list response doesn't include, so every card says "Other". With the marketplace, we maintain both sides.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Build your own when the list has to sit inside an existing settings page, mix in your own data, or look like nothing a theme can reach. Otherwise, don't own the page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Theming
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AutomationHubTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;IntegrationMarketplace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'@bytechef/embedded'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;cardColor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'#ffffff'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;enableColor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'#15803d'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;fontFamily&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Inter, sans-serif'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'light'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;primaryColor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'#2563eb'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;surfaceColor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'#f4f4f5'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;satisfies&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AutomationHubTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;IntegrationMarketplace&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;jwtToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jwtToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;satisfies&lt;/code&gt;, not a type annotation. The prop is typed &lt;code&gt;Record&amp;lt;string, unknown&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and TypeScript won't assign an interface-typed value to it. &lt;code&gt;satisfies&lt;/code&gt; checks every key and keeps the object's own type. Invalid colors are ignored, not fatal. Only &lt;code&gt;mode&lt;/code&gt; reaches the Connect dialog.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Gotchas
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Published isn't listed.&lt;/strong&gt; You need an &lt;em&gt;enabled&lt;/em&gt; configuration in the marketplace's environment. Check the switch before you debug the component.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Environment defaults to PRODUCTION.&lt;/strong&gt; The sample defaults to DEVELOPMENT. Set it explicitly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The card title isn't your Name field.&lt;/strong&gt; It's the component's display title. Your description does show.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Stuck spinner = handshake problem.&lt;/strong&gt; The iframe never got an &lt;code&gt;EMBED_INIT&lt;/code&gt; it trusts. Compare your origin, scheme and port included, with &lt;code&gt;BYTECHEF_EMBEDDED_ALLOWED_PARENT_ORIGINS&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;onConnectDialogClose&lt;/code&gt; is a hint.&lt;/strong&gt; It fires on connect, disconnect or dismiss, and in 0.4.0 it can fire twice. Make your handler idempotent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Connected doesn't mean healthy.&lt;/strong&gt; A card says Connected even when &lt;code&gt;credentialStatus&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;INVALID&lt;/code&gt;. Check it from your backend and warn users before a workflow fails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;One instance per card.&lt;/strong&gt; Connected opens the user's first instance. If you allow several per user, manage them from your own page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Before production
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set &lt;code&gt;BYTECHEF_EMBEDDED_ALLOWED_PARENT_ORIGINS&lt;/code&gt; to every embedding origin, and nothing else.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable a Production configuration per integration, with production OAuth credentials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pass &lt;code&gt;environment="PRODUCTION"&lt;/code&gt; explicitly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Refresh the JWT before it expires. The component re-sends &lt;code&gt;EMBED_INIT&lt;/code&gt; without a reload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sign in as a user on each plan and check each catalog. An expression error hides the integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set at least &lt;code&gt;mode&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;primaryColor&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;surfaceColor&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;fontFamily&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test the round trip per integration: connect, toggle a workflow, edit an input, disconnect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Enable a configuration for one of your integrations, upgrade to &lt;code&gt;@bytechef/embedded&lt;/code&gt; 0.4.0, run the embedded sample app, and open &lt;strong&gt;Integration Marketplace&lt;/strong&gt; next to &lt;strong&gt;Integrations&lt;/strong&gt;. Connect something in one and watch it turn Connected in the other.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Next in the series: &lt;strong&gt;Field Mapping&lt;/strong&gt;, the full story behind those &lt;code&gt;mapObjectFields&lt;/code&gt; callbacks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ByteChef is an open-source workflow automation and AI agent platform: &lt;a href="https://github.com/bytechefhq/bytechef" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;github.com/bytechefhq/bytechef&lt;/a&gt;. The full version of this post, with every request and response, is on &lt;a href="https://blog.bytechef.io/blogs/embedded-integration-marketplace" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;our blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


  TypeScript Const Assertions on Function Arguments in 2026: When Inline as const Beats a Generic Constraint
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This article was written with the assistance of AI, under human supervision and review.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Developers preserve literal types by adding generic constraints to function signatures. This forces every caller to satisfy the constraint, even when the function does not need narrower types. The function signature grows complex, and callers lose flexibility. When a route definition function demands a constraint like &lt;code&gt;T extends readonly string[]&lt;/code&gt;, teams must decide whether that constraint belongs in the signature or at the call site.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fywqeq01jeqdxa0abpv2r.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fywqeq01jeqdxa0abpv2r.png" width="799" height="184"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TypeScript 3.4 introduced const assertions with &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; syntax (documented in the &lt;a href="https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/release-notes/typescript-3-4" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TypeScript 3.4 release notes&lt;/a&gt;), allowing developers to freeze literal types at the expression level. When applied inline to function arguments, &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; narrows the type at the call site without changing the function signature. The function accepts the widened type, but the caller supplies a narrowed literal that TypeScript preserves through inference.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F0gfy5t86tu34lmy9st17.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F0gfy5t86tu34lmy9st17.png" width="799" height="184"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This pattern shifts type narrowing from the function's responsibility to the caller's control. The function signature stays simple. Callers who need narrow types add &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt;. Callers who prefer flexibility omit it. Teams avoid encoding every type requirement in the function signature itself.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Key Takeaways
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inline &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; on function arguments preserves literal types without changing the function signature, shifting narrowing control from function author to caller.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generic constraints like &lt;code&gt;T extends readonly string[]&lt;/code&gt; force every caller to satisfy the constraint even when the function logic works with widened types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applying &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; at the call site allows the function to accept both wide and narrow types, with callers choosing which behavior they need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combining const type parameters (&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;const T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; syntax in TypeScript 5.0+) with inline assertions provides granular control over which arguments narrow and which stay flexible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inline &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; breaks type inference when the compiler cannot unify the narrowed type with the function's expected parameter type, requiring explicit type annotations to resolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why Generic Constraints Fall Short for Literal Preservation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Generic constraints enforce type boundaries but do not preserve literal specificity. A constraint like &lt;code&gt;T extends string&lt;/code&gt; accepts both &lt;code&gt;"GET"&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;, yet the function's return type sees only the constraint's upper bound. The literal information vanishes.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;defineRoute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;extends&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;route&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;defineRoute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"GET"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// route.method has type string, not "GET"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The constraint ensures &lt;code&gt;method&lt;/code&gt; is a string, but TypeScript widens &lt;code&gt;"GET"&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt; during inference. The returned object loses the literal type. Discriminated unions, exhaustiveness checks, and autocomplete all depend on literal preservation. When the type widens, these features break.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F2j0h5vgvna9ounwz1trk.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F2j0h5vgvna9ounwz1trk.png" width="770" height="2594"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Adding &lt;code&gt;readonly&lt;/code&gt; to the constraint does not solve this. A constraint like &lt;code&gt;T extends readonly string[]&lt;/code&gt; still widens individual elements to &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;. The array becomes immutable, but the element types lose their literals. Teams often add both a constraint and a manual type assertion in the function body, creating redundant type logic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/release-notes/typescript-3-4" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TypeScript 3.4 release notes&lt;/a&gt; document const assertions as freezing literal types on simple expressions. Applying &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; to an object literal makes all properties &lt;code&gt;readonly&lt;/code&gt; and preserves each value's literal type. When applied to an array, the result becomes a &lt;code&gt;readonly&lt;/code&gt; tuple with literal element types. This behavior extends to function arguments when the assertion appears at the call site.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Inline as const on Function Arguments: Syntax and Mechanics
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Placing &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; on a function argument applies the assertion before the function receives the value. The caller freezes the type, and the function sees the narrowed result. The function signature itself does not change.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;registerHandler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;callback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// implementation&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;registerHandler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"click"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;event&lt;/code&gt; parameter accepts &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;, but the caller supplies &lt;code&gt;"click"&lt;/code&gt; narrowed to its literal type. TypeScript infers the argument as &lt;code&gt;"click"&lt;/code&gt;, not &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;. If the function's implementation uses &lt;code&gt;event&lt;/code&gt; in a discriminated union or passes it to another function expecting literals, the narrow type propagates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This syntax works with objects, arrays, and tuples:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;processConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;flags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// implementation&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;processConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"production"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;flags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"optimize"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"minify"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;config&lt;/code&gt; parameter accepts an object with &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;string[]&lt;/code&gt; properties. The caller passes an object with &lt;code&gt;mode: "production"&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;flags: readonly ["optimize", "minify"]&lt;/code&gt;. TypeScript preserves these literal types. The function signature did not require &lt;code&gt;readonly&lt;/code&gt; or literal constraints, yet the caller achieves the same narrowing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fsvpn7c04flv3zv7j83bo.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fsvpn7c04flv3zv7j83bo.jpg" alt="TypeScript const assertion syntax comparison" width="525" height="350"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;TypeScript const assertion syntax comparison&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/release-notes/typescript-3-4" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TypeScript 3.4 release notes&lt;/a&gt; state that const assertions apply only to simple literal expressions. Attempting to assert a computed value or conditional expression fails at compile time. The assertion must wrap the literal directly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Developers gain flexibility by choosing where to apply &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt;. A function accepting configuration objects can serve callers who need strict literals and callers who prefer dynamic values. The function author writes one signature. Callers who need narrow types add the assertion. Callers who do not need it omit the assertion and pass regular values.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Real-World Scenarios: Route Configs, Event Maps, and Discriminated Unions
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Route configuration functions demonstrate the pattern's value. A routing library accepts an array of route definitions. Each route has a method, path, and handler. The library's internal logic dispatches based on exact method strings like &lt;code&gt;"GET"&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;"POST"&lt;/code&gt;. If the method type widens to &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;, the dispatcher cannot narrow the union correctly.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;defineRoutes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;routes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Array&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;handler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;routes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;routes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;defineRoutes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"GET"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/users"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;handler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"POST"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/users"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;handler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// routes[0].method has type "GET", not string&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The function signature accepts &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt; for &lt;code&gt;method&lt;/code&gt;, but the caller applies &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; to the array. Each route's method preserves its literal type. The dispatcher can now narrow based on &lt;code&gt;route.method === "GET"&lt;/code&gt; without type guards.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fbolvmhysx83dejm7fdr8.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fbolvmhysx83dejm7fdr8.png" width="798" height="159"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Event maps follow the same pattern. A framework's event emitter accepts an object mapping event names to payload types. The emitter's &lt;code&gt;on&lt;/code&gt; method uses the map to enforce that listeners receive the correct payload. If event names widen to &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;, the map's keys lose their discriminating power.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createEmitter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;extends&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Record&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;K&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;extends&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;keyof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;K&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;listener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;K&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// implementation&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;emitter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createEmitter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;click&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;keypress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;emitter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"click"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// data has type { readonly x: 0; readonly y: 0 }&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;events&lt;/code&gt; parameter accepts any object, but the caller applies &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt;. Each event name becomes a literal, and each payload preserves its exact shape. The &lt;code&gt;on&lt;/code&gt; method's listener receives a narrowed &lt;code&gt;data&lt;/code&gt; parameter based on the event key.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Discriminated unions in state machines rely on literal types to distinguish variants. A state reducer accepts an action with a &lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt; field. The reducer switches on &lt;code&gt;action.type&lt;/code&gt; to handle each case. If &lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt; widens to &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;, the switch statement loses exhaustiveness checking.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;reducer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;State&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;switch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"increment"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"decrement"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;reducer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"increment"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;action&lt;/code&gt; parameter accepts &lt;code&gt;type: string&lt;/code&gt;, but the caller supplies &lt;code&gt;type: "increment"&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt;. The reducer's switch statement sees the literal type and narrows accordingly. TypeScript detects when a case is missing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These scenarios share a common need: the function logic operates on wide types, but downstream code requires narrow literals. Encoding the narrowness in the function signature forces every caller to satisfy it. Applying &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; at the call site shifts the responsibility to callers who need it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Generic Constraints vs Inline as const: When Each One Wins
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Generic constraints enforce invariants across all callers. When every invocation must satisfy a type requirement, the constraint belongs in the signature. Inline &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; grants flexibility. When some callers need narrow types and others do not, the assertion belongs at the call site.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Aspect&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Generic Constraint&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Inline as const&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Enforcement&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Mandatory for all callers&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Optional per call site&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Signature complexity&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Adds type parameters and bounds&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No signature change&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Type narrowing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Preserves constraint bound only&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Preserves exact literals&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Flexibility&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Uniform behavior&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Caller-controlled behavior&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Use case&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Invariants required by function logic&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Narrowing needed by caller logic&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A validation function that checks an array's contents requires a constraint. The function's implementation depends on the array being &lt;code&gt;readonly&lt;/code&gt; to avoid mutation during validation. Every caller must pass a &lt;code&gt;readonly&lt;/code&gt; array. The constraint enforces this.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;validate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;extends&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// implementation depends on immutability&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The constraint communicates to callers that mutation is forbidden. Attempting to pass a mutable array fails at compile time. This is a true invariant of the function's contract.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A formatting function that accepts a string does not require a constraint. The function's implementation works with any string, but some callers need to preserve the specific string literal for autocomplete or discriminated unions elsewhere. Those callers add &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;formatMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;template&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;template&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;/%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"value"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;formatMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"User %s logged in"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fr3jkzfm14nu78uj88uto.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fr3jkzfm14nu78uj88uto.jpg" alt="Generic constraints versus inline assertions comparison" width="525" height="350"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Generic constraints versus inline assertions comparison&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The function signature accepts &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt; because the implementation does not care about narrowness. Callers who need the literal type for other purposes add the assertion. Callers who do not need it pass a plain string.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fibd8o19uqldhywgwna40.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fibd8o19uqldhywgwna40.png" width="800" height="594"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Teams evaluate whether the narrowness benefits the function's implementation or the caller's context. If the function's logic requires it, use a constraint. If the caller's downstream code requires it, use &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; at the call site. When both need it, combine them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Combining Both: Const Type Parameters and Inline Assertions
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TypeScript 5.0 introduced const type parameters with the syntax &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;const T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. This signals that the type parameter should infer as narrow as possible without requiring &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; at the call site. The function signature requests narrow inference, but callers retain the option to override it.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"production"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;flags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"optimize"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// config has type { readonly mode: "production"; readonly flags: readonly ["optimize"] }&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;const T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; parameter tells TypeScript to infer &lt;code&gt;T&lt;/code&gt; with literal types. The caller passes a plain object without &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt;, yet the result preserves literals. This reverses the control: the function author requests narrow inference, and callers must opt out by explicitly widening the type.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Combining &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;const T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; with inline &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; provides granular control. A function accepting multiple parameters can request narrow inference for one parameter and allow wide inference for another. Callers apply &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; to specific arguments as needed.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;defineAction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;defineAction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"increment"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// action.type has type "increment"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// action.payload has type { readonly amount: 5 }&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt; parameter uses &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;const T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; to infer narrowly. The &lt;code&gt;payload&lt;/code&gt; parameter accepts &lt;code&gt;unknown&lt;/code&gt;, and the caller applies &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; to narrow its shape. The function signature remains concise. Callers control which parts narrow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This combination suits APIs where some arguments always need literals and others sometimes do. A router's path parameter always needs a literal string for type-safe route matching. The handler parameter might accept a plain function or a narrowed configuration object depending on the route's needs.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;route&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;handler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;handler&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;route&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/users/:id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// path has type "/users/:id"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;const P&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; parameter ensures &lt;code&gt;path&lt;/code&gt; always infers as a literal. Callers do not need to remember to add &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt;. The handler parameter stays flexible. When a caller needs to narrow the handler's configuration, they apply &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; to that argument only.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Developers apply this pattern selectively. Requesting narrow inference for every parameter makes the signature rigid. Applying it to parameters where narrowness benefits the function's type safety (like path patterns or discriminated union tags) keeps the API intuitive. Callers supply &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; for additional narrowing when their specific use case demands it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Common Pitfalls: When Inline as const Breaks Inference
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TypeScript's type inference engine attempts to unify the narrowed type with the function's expected parameter type. When the narrowed type contains properties or shapes the parameter type does not expect, inference fails. The compiler reports that the types are incompatible.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;processData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// implementation&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;processData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;42&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;extra&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"field"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Error: Object literal may only specify known properties&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;data&lt;/code&gt; parameter expects an object with a &lt;code&gt;value&lt;/code&gt; property of type &lt;code&gt;number&lt;/code&gt;. The caller supplies an object with an additional &lt;code&gt;extra&lt;/code&gt; property and applies &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt;. TypeScript narrows the object to &lt;code&gt;{ readonly value: 42; readonly extra: "field" }&lt;/code&gt;. This type does not match &lt;code&gt;{ value: number }&lt;/code&gt; because of the excess property. The function signature must explicitly allow excess properties or the caller must omit them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fyy56sj4lm9ph1snpp29w.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fyy56sj4lm9ph1snpp29w.png" width="800" height="241"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Applying &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; to computed values fails because the &lt;a href="https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/release-notes/typescript-3-4" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TypeScript 3.4 release notes&lt;/a&gt; restrict const assertions to simple literal expressions. Attempting to assert a function call or conditional expression produces a compile error.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;random&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.5&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"a"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"b"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Error: A 'const' assertion can only be applied to a string, number, boolean, array, or object literal&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The assertion must wrap the literal directly. Developers who need to narrow a computed value must assign it to a const variable first, then reference that variable. The variable declaration applies the assertion implicitly.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;random&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.5&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"a"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"b"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This syntax asserts each branch of the conditional separately. The resulting type is the union &lt;code&gt;"a" | "b"&lt;/code&gt;, which preserves both literals.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Deep nesting in object literals causes TypeScript's inference to slow down when &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; applies. Large configuration objects with many nested levels can trigger performance warnings. The compiler must traverse the entire structure to apply &lt;code&gt;readonly&lt;/code&gt; and preserve literals at every level. Teams break large objects into smaller const variables to avoid this.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;baseConfig&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"production"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;flags&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"optimize"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"minify"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;baseConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;flags&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Spreading const variables composes the final object without requiring a single assertion on a deeply nested structure. Each variable narrows independently, and the spread combines them. This approach scales better than applying &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; to a massive literal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Readonly properties in const-asserted objects prevent mutation but do not prevent reassignment of the object itself. A const-asserted array becomes a &lt;code&gt;readonly&lt;/code&gt; tuple, but the variable holding that array can still be reassigned unless declared with &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;routes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"GET"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;routes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"POST"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// allowed&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;routes&lt;/code&gt; variable is mutable. The array itself is &lt;code&gt;readonly&lt;/code&gt;, meaning you cannot push or modify elements, but reassigning the entire variable succeeds. Developers who need true immutability declare the variable with &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; in addition to applying &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; to the value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Understanding these pitfalls helps teams apply inline &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; correctly. The pattern works when the narrowed type remains compatible with the function's parameter type, when the assertion applies to a simple literal, and when performance remains acceptable. When these conditions hold, inline &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; provides type narrowing without signature complexity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Frequently Asked Questions
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  When should a function signature use a generic constraint instead of expecting callers to apply as const?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When the function's implementation depends on a type property that every caller must satisfy, encode it as a generic constraint. A validation function that iterates over a readonly array needs the constraint &lt;code&gt;T extends readonly unknown[]&lt;/code&gt; because mutation during iteration breaks the logic. When the function works with both wide and narrow types and only some callers need narrowness, omit the constraint and let callers apply &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; as needed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Does applying as const to a function argument change the runtime behavior?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No. Const assertions are a compile-time type annotation. The &lt;a href="https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/release-notes/typescript-3-4" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TypeScript 3.4 release notes&lt;/a&gt; clarify that &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; signals to the compiler that literal types should not widen. The compiled JavaScript code is identical to code without the assertion. The difference is purely in the type information TypeScript tracks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Can inline as const preserve literal types through multiple function calls?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes, as long as each function in the chain preserves the type. If the first function returns the narrowed value and the second function accepts it without widening, the literals propagate. Breaking the chain happens when an intermediate function's return type widens the value. Generic type parameters that preserve the input type (like &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;(value: T) =&amp;gt; T&lt;/code&gt;) maintain the chain.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  What is the difference between const type parameters in TypeScript 5.0 and inline as const?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Const type parameters (&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;const T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;) request narrow inference at the function signature level, applying to all callers by default. Inline &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; applies at the call site, giving each caller control over whether to narrow. Combining both allows the function to request narrow inference for specific parameters while letting callers selectively narrow others with inline assertions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Does as const work with rest parameters or variadic tuple types?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes. Applying &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; to an array passed as a rest parameter narrows it to a readonly tuple. The function signature must accept the tuple type, either through a generic constraint or by declaring the rest parameter with &lt;code&gt;readonly&lt;/code&gt;. When the function expects &lt;code&gt;...args: unknown[]&lt;/code&gt;, passing &lt;code&gt;...[1, 2, 3] as const&lt;/code&gt; preserves the tuple type &lt;code&gt;readonly [1, 2, 3]&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Choosing the Right Pattern for 2026
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Inline &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; on function arguments shifts type narrowing control from the function signature to the call site. Function authors write simpler signatures that accept wide types. Callers who need literal preservation add the assertion. Callers who prefer flexibility omit it. This pattern reduces signature complexity while maintaining type safety for callers who need it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Generic constraints still enforce invariants when every caller must satisfy a type requirement. Combining const type parameters with inline assertions provides granular control, allowing function authors to request narrow inference for some parameters while leaving others flexible. Teams evaluate whether narrowness benefits the function's logic or the caller's downstream code, then apply the appropriate pattern. When the function's implementation requires narrow types, use a constraint. When only some callers need them, use inline &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; at the call site.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Understanding when inference breaks (excess properties, computed values, deep nesting) prevents runtime surprises and keeps compile times manageable. As TypeScript's inference engine evolves, inline &lt;code&gt;as const&lt;/code&gt; remains a low-overhead pattern for preserving literal types without encoding every requirement in the function signature.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Sources
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/release-notes/typescript-3-4.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TypeScript: Documentation - TypeScript 3.4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rive is great at one thing Lottie and video can't do: the animation reacts. A button knows it's hovered, a mascot knows the user got the answer wrong, a progress ring knows it's at 73%.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But that power comes with a catch. A Rive file is not just artwork anymore. It's a small piece of your app's logic, and it has an API. And like any API, it breaks when the two sides didn't agree on the contract first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After 10+ years in motion design and a lot of Rive projects for product teams, I've noticed the same thing again and again: almost every "the animation doesn't work" message I get is not a bug. It's a missing agreement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So here's the checklist I go through with developers before I start animating. Steal it for your next project.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;1. State machine name&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your code loads the state machine by its exact name. State Machine 1 (the default) works, but it's easy to rename later and silently break everything.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Agree on one clear name early, for example Mascot SM or Button SM, and don't change it without telling each other.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;2. Input names and types&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the big one. Write the inputs down like an API spec:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;isHover (Boolean): the pointer is over the element&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;isPressed (Boolean): the element is being pressed&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;success (Trigger): plays the celebration once&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;progress (Number, 0–100): fills the progress ring&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Names are case-sensitive. isHover and IsHover are two different inputs, and the runtime won't warn you loudly when you get it wrong. You'll just get… nothing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;3. Who owns the logic?&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Decide what lives in the Rive file and what lives in your code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Inside Rive: transitions, blending, idle loops, "after the celebration go back to idle".&lt;br&gt;
Inside your app: when something happens (API response, user action, timer).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A simple rule that works: the app sends facts ("the answer was correct"), the Rive file decides how it looks. That way the animator can improve the motion later without touching your code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;4. Inputs vs. Data Binding&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Newer Rive runtimes support Data Binding (view models), which is often a cleaner way to push data like text, numbers and colors into an animation than wiring up lots of separate inputs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before work starts, check which runtime version your app uses and agree on one approach. Mixing both "because the file had it" is how projects get messy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;5. Artboard size and how it should scale&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tell your animator where the animation will live: a 48px icon, a full-width hero, a card on mobile?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then agree on the fit and alignment you'll use in code (Contain, Cover, Fill, etc.). An artboard designed for Cover will look cropped if you render it with Contain, and the other way round.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;6. Default state on load&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What should the user see in the first frame? This matters more than people think, because it's what shows while everything else loads.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Agree that the state machine starts in a clean, meaningful idle state, not halfway through an intro animation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;7. Events coming back to your app&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rive can also talk back to your code with Rive Events, for example "the celebration finished" or "the user clicked the mascot's hat".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you need to know when something ends (to show the next screen, play a sound, log analytics), ask for an event. Don't guess the duration with a setTimeout. The day the animator makes the motion 200ms snappier, your timing breaks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;8. Text and fonts&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the animation contains text that changes (a username, a score, a translated label), say so up front. Runtime text needs to be set up differently than text that's baked into the artwork, and embedded fonts add to the file size.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also think about localization: German words are long. Make sure the layout survives them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;9. File size and performance budget&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rive files are usually tiny, but they can grow with embedded raster images, fonts and lots of artboards.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Give your animator a budget (for example "under 150 KB for the onboarding mascot") and the lowest device you need to support. It changes how the file gets built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;10. A test page before the real integration&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before the file goes into the app, I always share a quick preview where the developer can toggle every input and fire every trigger by hand.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It takes minutes and catches most problems: wrong input names, transitions that never fire, states that get stuck.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What the integration looks like when the contract is clear&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here's a minimal React example using @rive-app/react-canvas. Notice how little code there is when the names were agreed on in advance:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;useRive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;useStateMachineInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Layout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Fit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Alignment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@rive-app/react-canvas"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;STATE_MACHINE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Button SM"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;RiveButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;rive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;RiveComponent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/animations/button.riv"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;stateMachines&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;STATE_MACHINE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;autoplay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;layout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Layout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Fit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Contain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;alignment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Alignment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Center&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;isHover&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useStateMachineInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;rive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;STATE_MACHINE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"isHover"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useStateMachineInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;rive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;STATE_MACHINE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"success"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;RiveComponent&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;240&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;80&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cursor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"pointer"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;onMouseEnter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;isHover&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;isHover&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;onMouseLeave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;isHover&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;isHover&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fire&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Three names (&lt;strong&gt;Button SM&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;isHover&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;success&lt;/strong&gt;) and the whole thing works. Get one letter wrong and nothing happens. That's why the checklist exists.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The copy-paste version&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Send this to your animator (or developer) before the project starts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;RIVE HANDOFF AGREEMENT&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;State machine name:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inputs (name / type / purpose):&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inputs or Data Binding? Runtime + version:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logic owned by Rive / owned by app:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Artboard size + Fit/Alignment in code:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Default state on load:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Events needed back in the app:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dynamic text / fonts / languages:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;File size budget + lowest target device:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preview/test page before integration: yes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ten lines, ten minutes, and you'll skip most of the back-and-forth that makes Rive projects drag on.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  &lt;strong&gt;Need a Rive animator who works this way?&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm Maxim, a Rive animator and motion designer with 10+ years of experience and 100+ projects. I create interactive mascots, animated logos and icons, UI micro-interactions and onboarding animations, and every file comes with clean, documented inputs your developers can plug in right away.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;👉 See my work and get a quote at &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://hireriveanimator.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;hireriveanimator.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Questions about your own Rive setup? Drop them in the comments and I'll answer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The agent adds a “Back to settings” control as &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a href="/settings"&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. The app already has a &lt;code&gt;Link&lt;/code&gt; (or &lt;code&gt;RouterLink&lt;/code&gt;, or Next.js &lt;code&gt;Link&lt;/code&gt;) that prefetches, keeps the client transition, and applies the active class from the design system. The raw anchor does a full reload, loses draft state on the page, and looks unstyled for a frame.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I’ve started treating &lt;strong&gt;a raw &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; to an internal path as a merge question&lt;/strong&gt;, not as a finished navigation change. External URLs, &lt;code&gt;mailto:&lt;/code&gt;, and file downloads can stay anchors. In-app paths should go through the shared component.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why the raw anchor sneaks in
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The model has seen millions of HTML examples. &lt;code&gt;href="/settings"&lt;/code&gt; looks correct, and it will work in the preview. What it will not do is honor the app’s scroll restoration, locale prefix, base path, or analytics hook that lives on &lt;code&gt;Link&lt;/code&gt;. A new tab target also disappears: the shared component may already set it, or may explicitly forbid it for internal routes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A full reload on an internal click is easy to miss in a happy-path click-through and expensive in a form or a wizard.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  A simple navigation policy
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal paths use the shared &lt;code&gt;Link&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;External URLs use &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (or the shared &lt;code&gt;ExternalLink&lt;/code&gt; if you have one), with &lt;code&gt;rel&lt;/code&gt; set the way the app already sets it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Do not invent a second wrapper&lt;/strong&gt; to “add prefetch”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Hash links and in-page anchors follow the existing pattern&lt;/strong&gt;, not a new one-off &lt;code&gt;onClick&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the repo has a lint rule for this (&lt;code&gt;@next/next/no-html-link-for-pages&lt;/code&gt;, a custom ESLint check), paste the rule into the prompt. If it does not, a one-line review grep for &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a href="/&lt;/code&gt; is enough.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What to put in the prompt
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight markdown"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Internal routes must use the existing Link component (see src/components/Link or next/link).
Do not add a raw &amp;lt;a&amp;gt; for an in-app path.
External URLs, mailto, and file downloads may use &amp;lt;a&amp;gt;, with the existing rel/target helpers.
Do not invent a new NavLink or PrefetchLink.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;In review, search the diff for &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a&lt;/code&gt;. Each hit should be external, a download, or justified. If the href is a path the router owns, send it back.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Reject / send back
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reject&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a href="/dashboard"&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; in a page that already imports &lt;code&gt;Link&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A new &lt;code&gt;SmartLink&lt;/code&gt; helper when &lt;code&gt;Link&lt;/code&gt; already exists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An in-app anchor that forces &lt;code&gt;target="_blank"&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A click handler that &lt;code&gt;window.location.href =&lt;/code&gt; to an internal path&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accept&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;Link&lt;/code&gt; (or the repo’s named wrapper) for in-app paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A raw anchor for an external docs URL, with the existing &lt;code&gt;rel&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine download link that the shared &lt;code&gt;Link&lt;/code&gt; does not support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
